.TH AVR\-SERVICE\-TOKEN\-SET\-ACCESS 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-service-token-set-access \- Replace a service token's grants or change its VM creation.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr service-token set-access
[OPTIONS] TOKEN_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace a service token's grants or change its VM creation.
.PP
Grant options (--repo, --firewall-rule, --all-firewall-rules, --vm and --all-vms) replace every grant the token holds: a grant you leave out is removed, so repeat the ones to keep. Without grant options the grants stay. The maximum of owned VMs stays unless --max-owned-vms or --no-vm-create changes it. When the change removes or lowers a grant or VM creation, the command lists what goes and asks first; without a terminal it then refuses unless --yes is given. It reads the token first and the change fails if its access changes in between. A grant that widens its access must be within your own access now. The API may ask for a recent sign-in; the command then exits 4 and says to sign in again. The change applies to the token's next request.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr service-token set-access <token-id> --repo acme/api --repo acme/web
    avr service-token set-access <token-id> --all-firewall-rules --yes
    avr service-token set-access <token-id> --max-owned-vms 10
    avr service-token set-access <token-id> --no-vm-create
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fITOKEN_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR, \fB\-R\fR \fITEXT\fR
Grant read access to a repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-firewall\-rule\fR \fITEXT\fR
Grant read access to an egress firewall rule, by rule ID (efr-xxx). Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-firewall\-rules\fR
Grant read access to every egress firewall rule, including rules added later.
.TP
\fB\-\-vm\fR \fITEXT\fR
Grant access to a VM, by VM ID (cvm-xxx): read, or write with cvm-xxx:write. Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-vms\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Grant read or write access to every VM of the organization, including VMs created later. (choices: read, write)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-owned\-vms\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Let the token create VMs and own up to this many at once; deleting a VM frees a place. A token of the root group cannot create VMs. Lowering it keeps the VMs the token owns. Omit to keep the current maximum.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-vm\-create\fR
Stop the token creating VMs; its grants stay unless grant options are given. It keeps administering the VMs it created.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Apply the change without asking, even when it removes or lowers access.
.SH SEE ALSO
